WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.720
The oldest memory I have is
of me smiling with my beloved mother.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:15.240
But it wasn’t me who was with my mother.
It was my deceased older sister, Alicia.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.920
I was then born with Alicia’s memories.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.100
But in the end, I was unable to become her.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:26.820
My mother ended up not taking my hand.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.000
Leaving a somewhat lonely feeling behind, she left me.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.040
I don’t want my kids to have those same feelings.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.040
But I...

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:05.960
The things that I can do for you and no one else

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.660
I honestly feel and wish for those

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.380
I am frozen by uncertainties

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:24.620
By the rules I have been relying on

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.320
My past embellished with excuses

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.520
I want to get over it

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.800
Staining the stars in heaven scarlet

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.270
Gather the grains of miracles

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:44.530
Before the still, unseen night

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.810
I want to tell you that I am escaping from illusions

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.990
The twilight moon calls out to me

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.080
Removing my veil of delusions

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.290
My hidden, deceitful self

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.170
And took all of my weaknesses

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:07.630
I don’t want words that seem passionate

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:17.050
The fact that I’m here right now is my truth

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.190
We weren’t able to protect them again.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.820
Twenty-five dead. Twenty-one of those were civilians.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.390
There really are too many crimes on Mid.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.310
We don’t have enough men or firepower.
We’re lacking in everything.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.010
This time the damned Navy managed to overlook a criminal mage.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:55.220
Yet, all of the firepower and gifted mages
are taken by the Main Office.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.230
It’s not that I don’t understand the Navy’s problems.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.480
Over there, the scope of
the incidents they deal with is different.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.640
Does that mean that it’s okay to ignore
when a small area of a small planet is destroyed?

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.670
I’m sorry.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:16.590
I do not carry any magical powers like you do,
nor do I have the power to teach people.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:24.080
But at least if I can rise in the ranks of the Bureau and collect power, we might be able to change this.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.010
For you, it may very well be possible.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.920
We need a revolution!

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.400
If you leave peace and justice in this city to my hands,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:44.090
I can guarantee a higher level of security for each person.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.990
A rise in the functionality of the regulation system.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.100
Amazing results!

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.610
But regarding that system,
the Main Office has said there’s been a problem.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.240
Tell them to deal with it themselves.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.280
Those people have no concept of justice on the surface.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.240
It’s amazing how hard you’ve worked.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:07.370
Taking into account your impeccable sense of justice,
we have something to ask of you.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.270
Regius, I’ve been hearing
some not-so-good rumors about you lately.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.500
I’m not doing anything different.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:18.000
The Ground Armed Service
has been gaining strength on Mid.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:23.450
Your unit seems to be investigating
the Combat Cyborg Incident, correct?

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.890
That’s correct.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.080
I should have more important things for you to do.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.500
I’ll give it to you in the morning.
That will be your priority from then on.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:40.230
Nakajima, Alpine. We’re going to conduct our raid earlier than planned.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.620
We go tonight.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:44.620
Make sure you’re ready.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.090
Roger.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.060
Seems that we were right.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.480
This is a combat cyborg plant.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:58.860
Deputy captain, this is Team C.
The captain was protecting us, and...

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.060
So, they managed to get in this far.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.030
We’ll have to distance ourself from this base, as well.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.270
That’s too bad.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.670
Let’s take the corpse.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:22.590
At least, he’ll serve some purpose as the Doctor’s research sample.

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.360
Thanks a lot, Lt. General Gaiz.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.680
You let one of our important facilities get destroyed.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.100
Seems that my order didn’t get there in time.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.300
Well, no matter. There wasn’t that much damage anyway.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:42.020
Oh yeah, one more thing. Your dream,
the combat cyborgs, just proved their excellent skill.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.700
One-on-one, they took down
an S rank knight. Pretty awesome, right?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:54.850
Among the Bureau members we took, there are people who could be adapted as artificial mage samples.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:59.000
Zest Grangeitz, Mégane Alpine.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:03.950
Also, Mégane had a daughter.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.030
I’d like to secure her as a base for an artificial mage.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:11.350
Sure, we’ll take care of it.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.420
Should we tell Regius about this?

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.020
No.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.980
We’ll need to put him under
our complete control eventually.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:24.900
Zest Grangeitz may become a useful pawn to us.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.360
I want to ask you this.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:39.040
I was prepared to sacrifice myself for your justice,
but for whose sake did my men die?

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:42.960
Why did it turn out this way?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.880
The planet we wanted to protect.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.550
The power we wanted.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.510
The justice you and I dreamed of.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:56.140
When did it turn into something like this?

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:05.710
Why?!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.120
I thank you for playing your part.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:22.000
You’re just a hindrance to the Doctor’s plans.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.840
Zest, I...

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.630
I...

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.800
Regius.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:37.920
Now, your usefulness and your revenge
have come to an end.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:42.350
It’s always this way. I’m always too late.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.400
Sir.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.330
Did you...?

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:08.550
That’s right,

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.010
I did it.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.970
I was too weak and too late.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:30.780
Didn’t Tre tell you once?
That we were like father and daughter.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:40.900
Your mother, Presea Testarossa, was indeed a talented mage.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:45.940
She perfected the cloning technology that I created.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:50.380
But you were a failure to her.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:56.480
You were nothing like her biological daughter,
Alicia, who she wanted to revive.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.600
You were just a defective copy.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:06.980
So you didn’t get a real name.
You were just given the name of the project.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:12.470
The first product of the memory-transfer cloning technology, Project Fate.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.400
Fate Testarossa.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.050
Fate?

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.710
There’s no reason for us to fight, Lu.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:28.130
Nothing will come of it.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:32.590
Galue, if you’re a warrior who protects his mistress, stop Lu.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:37.790
Lu’s being tricked by them. She’s just being controlled.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:40.260
You don’t understand.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.320
I had people who were nice to me.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.730
I had friends.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:53.440
Everyone I care about is forgetting me.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.360
I don’t want to be alone.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:16.300
I’m tired of being lonely.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.880
I don’t want to be alone!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.160
Caro!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.150
Great, grand howl which pierces the skies above,

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.640
that which eternally guards distant land.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.300
Come forth, join me, and stand beside us now,

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.110
o jet black flame, protector of the land.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:52.630
We are very much alike, Lu and us.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:11:00.010
We were both always alone,
with no one to protect us, no one to believe in.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.290
Nothing made sense.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:07.520
And we couldn’t do anything but hurt things.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.000
But that can change.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.190
With just one chance, just one feeling,

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:16.480
We can change it!

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.350
<b>Summoning Dragon Mount</b>

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.920
An imperial, thunderous roar.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:27.220
<b>Come forth, Voltaire!</b>

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:43.540
We will definitely help with finding your mother.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:45.720
I promise.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.790
Stop doing this.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:49.380
You’re lying.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:50.700
I’m not lying.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:51.880
You’re lying.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:55.020
You’re lying!

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:15.440
Hakuten-Oh, Galue, kill them.
Kill the people who are in my way.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:16.880
Everyone. All of them!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.510
Galue.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.840
Kill them!

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.120
Galue!

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.500
Boosted Protection

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:51.200
It’s wrong to make your precious summons suffer.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.670
Galue and Hakuten-Oh are crying.

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:10.080
Erio.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.930
Jirai-Oh!

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:35.540
Fried!

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.750
<b>Blast Ray</b>

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.450
Fire!

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:48.930
Lu.

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:19.480
<b>Glittering Swordflash</b>

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:34.770
Caro.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.790
I managed, somehow.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.820
The summons are getting all confused.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.240
Is it because Lu is still trying to fight?

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.120
<b>Riot</b>

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.540
Riot Blade

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.980
Is that your final trump card?

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.620
No matter.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:24.900
Seems the A.M.F. is draining you.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.350
But are you sure it’s okay to use that?

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:34.940
Even if you defeat me here,
you can’t stop my creations and the <i>Cradle.</i>

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:38.910
If you use Project F the right way, it’s pretty helpful, isn’t it?

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:46.250
A copy of me already exists within
the wombs of each of the twelwe combat cyborgs.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:50.200
If just one of them survives, then I’ll come back.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.220
And in just one month,
they’ll be revived with my memories.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.210
That’s ridiculous.

00:15:56.210 --> 00:16:01.640
In the old era, the era of Alhazred,
this was everyday technology.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:15.990
In other words, if you can’t kill me <i>and</i> all twelve of my combat cyborgs, you can’t stop me or my plan.

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:22.640
Have you fallen into despair?

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:26.130
You and I are quite similar.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:37.180
The organic weapons that I’ve made myself,
and that which you sought, the children who can’t deny you.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:43.140
That which you have formed in your own way, and that which you are using for your own means.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.830
Shut up.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:53.640
Am I wrong?

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:59.450
You raised them so they cannot deny you and made them fight.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:03.400
Just like me, and your mother as well.

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:07.480
Everyone around you is nothing more
than a tool that you can use.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:12.840
And yet, you’re terrified that
the love they direct at you is fading.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:17.760
Your mother was like that as well.
You will also become like that, eventually.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:22.980
Terrified of making a mistake,
clinging to your weak bonds and shaking in terror.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:26.840
Don’t you think a life like that is without meaning?

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:27.580
You’re wrong!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.380
It’s not meaningless.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:33.350
We chose our own path.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:38.320
We had no place to go,
and Fate found us a warm home.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.640
She gave us tons of kindness.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:45.290
She taught us the happiness of protecting what’s important to us.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.190
She helped us and protected us.

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:51.210
At Riot Force 6, we were trained by Nanoha.

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:55.130
And we finally were able to try to stand and walk by ourselves.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:58.120
Fate isn’t wrong about anything.

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.580
If she’s in doubt, then we will be right there by her side.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.850
If she’s in trouble, we’ll be right there to save her.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:08.580
If she, for some reason, is wrong,
we’ll be there to scold her and then return back to her.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.720
We—all of us are here for her.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:15.190
So, don’t give up. Don’t hesitate.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.340
Fight!

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.640
Get set.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:27.540
Overdrive. Complete Sonic Form.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.240
Sonic Drive

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:38.280
Sorry, and thank you, Erio, Caro.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.340
There’s nothing to doubt, right?

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:45.760
Riot Zanber

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:52.140
Because I was weak,
I hesitated and let my worries get to me.

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:55.100
I will probably always fall into this pattern.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.190
But,

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:58.340
that’s fine.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.830
Because all of that makes me who I am.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.610
Her mana values have increased?

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.740
I’ve been searching for you, Miss.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:24.110
Scaglietti’s other brain
and the leader of the twelve combat cyborgs,

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:26.060
Number I, Uno.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:30.120
Shall I take a peak inside of your mind?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.150
Unie? This is bad.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.320
<b>I.S.: Deep Diver</b>

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:39.220
I won’t let you run.

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:47.200
Windenschaft!

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:57.630
She has movement magic?

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.650
<b>Gale Burst</b>

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.550
That armor is weak.

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.830
You’ll go down if you’re hit.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.860
<b>Ride Impulse</b>

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:06.470
Magnificent. You truly are magnificent.

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:10.160
I wanted this power.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:14.820
But the cost of capturing me
is that you’re going to be stuck here.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:18.750
You can’t stop the dream I entrusted to the <i>Cradle!</i>

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:42.180
Large-scale interdimensional criminal, Jail Scaglietti.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:45.400
I hereby place you under arrest.

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.320
There’s been a communication from Scaglietti’s hideout from Inspector Acous.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:54.040
A confirmation on the last position of the combat cyborgs, as well as their current operational status, has been received!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:58.920
It seems like the only ones left
are Number IV in the ship and you.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:02.240
I don’t know what you’ve been through,

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:07.160
but if you recognize your crimes and turn yourself in,
I think you’ll be allowed a fresh start.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.890
No way that’ll happen.

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:10.870
We’re combat cyborgs.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:12.540
Weapons for the purpose of fighting.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:17.060
There’s no other way of life for us
other than fighting and winning!

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.340
Snipe Shot

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.500
Even weapons that exist only for fighting
can laugh and live as kind people.

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.860
You may have been born a combat cyborg, but

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.220
I know a girl who’s more human than anyone,
who’s sweet to the point of stupidity, and who tries her best.

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:54.210
Stars 4 has captured Number IX.

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:57.180
Number IV is the only remaining combat cyborg.

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:03.020
They’re all complete losers.

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:10.640
Well, it’ll all work out if I’m around.

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:14.160
Isn’t that right, Doctor?

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:22.980
Their final trump card should soon be smashed to pieces, anyway.

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:25.210
The <i>Cradle</i> will reach

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:25.710
orbit in

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:26.040
1

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:26.660
1 hour

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:27.330
1 hour and 35 minutes

00:25:17.360 --> 00:25:19.460
Only a small amount
of time remains

00:25:19.460 --> 00:25:20.940
before the Cradle<i>
reaches its orbital position.</i>

00:25:20.940 --> 00:25:24.660
The final battle will take place just beneath the light of the stars.

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:33.980
Toward your true feelings, take off.
